== Problem 1: shortest s-t path with exactly one negative edge u->v (no negative cycle)
OK   random graphs with one negative edge: Bellman-Ford == exhaustive simple-path search (a shortest walk is a simple path, so it uses u->v at most once)  [6000 graphs]
OK   Solution 1: min{d_s(t), d_s(u) + w(u->v) + d_v(t)} from two Dijkstra runs in G - (u->v) == Bellman-Ford, every source/target pair  [26888 pairs, 5358 of them answered through u->v]
OK   Solution 1: the rebuilt walk (pred path to u, u->v, pred path from v; or pred path to t) goes from s to t, has the computed length, and with ties to d_s(t) is a simple path
OK   one-run variant: Dijkstra in the two-layer graph, crossing edge of weight 0, then + w(u->v) == Bellman-Ford
OK   Solution 2: the book's Dijkstra on G unmodified computes every distance correctly (any tie-breaking)
OK   Solution 2: every vertex is extracted at most twice, the tail u at most once  [max extractions of one vertex: 2; graphs with a vertex extracted twice: 439]
OK   Solution 2: the extracted keys decrease at most once, from the extraction of u to the extraction of v right after it  [2994 drops in 6000 runs]
OK   Solution 2: every extraction after u's extraction (all of them if u is never extracted) has its final distance
OK   Solution 2: ExtractMin <= 2V and relaxations <= 2E; Insert + DecreaseKey = relaxations + 1
OK   Solution 2: predecessor paths are shortest simple paths
OK   the bound 'twice' is attained, and a target can leave the queue first with a wrong distance (no early stop at its first extraction)  [targets extracted twice: 556, first key wrong: 556]
OK   NonnegativeDijkstra (a finished vertex is never scanned again) is wrong on some of these graphs  [452 of 6000 graphs]
OK   a heap with stale copies (skip a popped key > dist) makes exactly the same extractions as Insert/DecreaseKey
OK   adversarial graphs (zero-weight cycles, |w(u->v)| up to the limit set by the cycles through u->v, fixed and random tie-breaking): all three solutions correct, extraction bounds hold  [0 failures]
OK   growing random graphs (E = 4V, w(u->v) = -d_v(u), the most negative allowed): ExtractMin <= 2V, relaxations <= 2E, correct  [V=200: ExtractMin/V=1.03 (10 vertices twice), relax/E=0.40; V=800: ExtractMin/V=1.00 (16 vertices twice), relax/E=0.34; V=3200: ExtractMin/V=1.09 (341 vertices twice), relax/E=0.37]
